.context/
# .playtest/ is committed, not ignored: .playtest/<Game>/routes/ holds the deep
# starts a round ships (#362), and a fresh checkout needs them the way it needs the
# focus files. The old backstop that ignored all of .playtest/ guarded against a
# stray scratch directory — play-test *scratch* still belongs under
# .context/playtest/, and anything under .playtest/ that is not a route or a round
# record is a bug worth noticing rather than hiding.
# .claude/settings.json is tracked — it allowlists the play-test harness's own
# commands so a round doesn't stall on twenty permission prompts. Personal
# overrides belong in the local file, which is not.
.claude/settings.local.json
.dev-tooling
.DS_Store
.github/swift-format-matcher.json
.swift-format
.netrc
.swiftpm
/.build
/Packages
DerivedData/
# Package.resolved is not tracked for this package — dependencies resolve from
# the version ranges in Package.swift, and the dev-only tooling (docc, Persnicket)
# would otherwise churn it. The template resolves its own too.
/Package.resolved
bin/templates/Package.resolved
xcuserdata/
.build
# A traits-off build (`--disable-default-traits`, the configuration `bin/export-game`
# and the release workflows ship) gets its own scratch directory. Sharing `.build`
# would evict the ordinary build's artifacts every time and hand `bin/gnusto-mcp` a
# server-less binary its mtime gate has no reason to rebuild.
/.build-notraits
# Exported game binaries produced by bin/export-game.
/dist
# The rendered DocC site. Not `docs/`, which is hand-written and tracked: the
# plugin deletes its --output-path before writing, so pointing it at docs/ costs
# you twenty design documents.
/.docs-build
# Bytecode from bin/atlas/, the Dungeon atlas generator.
__pycache__/
